From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:28:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] --stdio: svxconnect as the helper of a host program that
 is the interface

A radio's GUI or a panel starts svxconnect --stdio with its own socket as
stdin and stdout. It sends the control FIFO's commands (app_control, through
ctl_dispatch_line), and is told in a line whatever it shows when it changes:
the connection, the talkgroup and the lock, the watched talkgroups with their
priorities, who is talking where, the recent overs, our transmission and why
one was refused or ended, the certificate, the banner. The log goes to
stderr. Over a SOCK_SEQPACKET socket the audio crosses in records of its own
when built with AUDIO=pipe. src/hostio.h has the whole exchange.

--cert-status prints the certificate's state on one line of key=value, for a
program that shows the enrolment.
