+### Under a host program: `--stdio`
+
+A program that is the user interface itself (a radio's own screen, a panel)
+runs `svxconnect --stdio` as its helper, with one of its sockets as stdin and
+stdout. It sends the control FIFO's commands, and gets a line whenever
+something it shows changes: the connection, the talkgroup and the lock, the
+watched talkgroups with their priorities, who is talking where, the recent
+overs, our own transmission (and why one was refused or ended), the
+certificate. The log goes to stderr. Over a `SOCK_SEQPACKET` socket the audio
+crosses too, 16 kHz mono in records of its own, when svxconnect is built with
+`make AUDIO=pipe`: then there is no sound card at all, and the host plays and
+records. The whole exchange is described in [src/hostio.h](src/hostio.h).
+
+`svxconnect --cert-status` prints the certificate's state on one line
+(`status=valid usable=1 request=0 not_after=... renew_at=... days=...`), for a
+program that shows the enrolment.
+
 ## Building and testing
 
 ```sh
@@ -253,6 +270,7 @@ make check      # the above, plus the client against a fake reflector (about a m
 make check-tsan # make check under ThreadSanitizer   (in build-tsan/)
 make check-asan # make check under ASan + UBSan      (in build-asan/)
 make asan       # AddressSanitizer + UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer build
+make AUDIO=pipe # the audio through a host program (--stdio), no sound card
 ```
 
 Dependencies: OpenSSL 3, libopus, ncurses. Audio needs no development package
